With KURU = 800 and ISLAK = 350, a raw value of 500 was read. What does the code below print to the serial monitor?

```
int yuzde = map(500, 800, 350, 0, 100);
Serial.println(yuzde);
```

The rain sensor is on A0 and the water level sensor is on A1. The readings are A0 = 700 and A1 = 450. What does this code print?

```
int yagmur = analogRead(A0);
int seviye = analogRead(A1);
Serial.print(yagmur < 600 ? "VAR" : "YOK");
Serial.print(" ");
if (seviye < 300) Serial.println("BOS");
else if (seviye < 600) Serial.println("ORTA");
else Serial.println("DOLU");
```

When the soil is wet and the raw value is 350, you expect 100 % on the screen, but this code prints 0 %. The KURU raw value is 800 and the ISLAK raw value is 350. Which line has the bug?

```
1 const int KURU = 800;
2 const int ISLAK = 350;
3 int yuzde = map(analogRead(A2), ISLAK, KURU, 0, 100);
4 Serial.println(yuzde);
```
